  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sunil Dnyaneshwar More vs The State Of Maharashtra on 14 October, 2021 Author: Revati Mohite Dere Bench: Revati Mohite Dere 8a. Ba 34 Digitally signed by Rupali Rupali Rajesh Rajesh Wakodikar Wakodikar Date: 2021.10.14 15:33:49 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay +0530 Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Bail Application No. 3484 Of 2021 Sunil Dnyaneshwar More ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. P.G.Chavan for the Applicant. Coram : Revati Mohite Dere, J. Date : 14th October, 2021",
    "facts": "1 3. By this application, the applicant seeks his enlargement in connection with C.R. No. 570/2021 registered with the Pandharpur Taluka Police Station, Solapur, for the alleged offences punishable Wakodikar 8a. BA 3484-2021. Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 59 r/w 3(1)(zz)(iii) of Food Safety and Standards Act. According to the complainant-Bharath Bhosale, the Foods Safety Officer, Food and Drugs Department, Solapur, on 8th September 2021, he along with the police staff, visited Panchwati Paan Shop at Sargam Chowk, Pandharpur, Solapur. In the search that was carried out, paan masala and supari worth Rs. 605/- was seized. The applicant is stated to be the owner of the said Panchwati Paan Shop. 5. Having regard to the facts, prima facie, it is doubtful whether an offence under Section 328 is disclosed qua the applicant.",
    "arguments": "",
